  "notes": "Neuro is where the drum & bass kick moves: 1, then 2a — the last 16th before beat 3 — against snares that never leave 2 and 4. Jump-up puts that second kick on the 3 and liquid on the and-of-3, and the one 16th between them is most of the difference. Everything else is sound design: six percussion lanes of clicks, rims, metal and reverses under a continuous 16th hat, harmony that barely moves (a static i with the occasional bII stab), and a Reese bass that is edited rather than held — the detune is in the sound, the movement is in the cell shapes, and the line reshuffles under a harmony that will not.",
